(footprint "NFC_Loop_35x27mm_4T_TUNE"
	(version 20260206)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "10.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "PROTOTYPE/TUNE REQUIRED: 13.56 MHz rectangular PCB loop for PN532, 4 turns on F.Cu, nominal copper envelope 35 x 27 mm, 0.50 mm trace / 0.50 mm gap, approximately 0.434 m copper length, first-order L estimate roughly 1.0 to 1.4 uH and DC resistance roughly 0.4 to 0.6 ohm for 35 um copper. Pads 1 and 2 are intentionally joined through the loop as a KiCad net tie. Inner end returns through a plated pad and short B.Cu crossover. The 36 x 29 mm embedded all-copper-layer keepout reserves the antenna field from foreign tracks, vias, pads, pours and footprints except for minimal relief immediately around the footprint's own three pads. Final PN532 matching values MUST be established on assembled hardware with a VNA because PCB stackup/etch, solder mask, battery/enclosure/hand proximity and nearby metal change inductance, Q, resonance and differential impedance.")
	(tags "NFC RFID PN532 13.56MHz loop antenna net tie prototype VNA tuning")
